 strategy allows you to clear your hand systematically.\n\nReason:\nYou hold three low singles (3, 5, Q) and three high control cards (2, 2, Red Joker). To win, you must cover your losing cards with your winning cards. Keeping the 2s separate gives you three separate chances to regain control (two 2s and the Joker), which exactly matches the number of low cards you need to smuggle through. Playing the pair of 2s would leave you short on re-entries. Start with the lowest single.\n\nAnswer:\n{"cards": ["♥3"]}'}
